UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 4, Week 12, Lesson 1: Australia and its neighbours in Asia and the Pacific', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Australia’s neighbours in Asia and the Pacific include countries and island nations across water borders. Neighbours are identified with atlases; relationships include trade, travel and shared environments.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same HSIE idea to a new place or source, then compare two pieces of evidence for strength.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nUsing an atlas, name three neighbouring countries or territories of Australia and the water body that separates Australia from one of them.\n\nFEEDBACK\nAnswers depend on the atlas (e.g. Indonesia, PNG, New Zealand); water e.g. Timor Sea / Coral Sea / Tasman Sea as appropriate.\n\nWATCH FOR\nCalling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nMake a neighbours fact strip: five places from an atlas with direction from Australia and one shared link (trade, sport, environment). Cite the atlas.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one source or idea you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"HSIE","learning_intention":"Australia’s neighbours in Asia and the Pacific include countries and island nations across water borders. Neighbours are identified with atlases; relationships include trade, travel and shared environments.","lesson_number":1,"lesson_role":"Investigate","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: local map, photo or interview notes"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["HS2-GEO-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Make a neighbours fact strip: five places from an atlas with direction from Australia and one shared link (trade, sport, environment). Cite the atlas. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: original example using neighbour on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample error: Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood.. Correction: Answers depend on the atlas (e.g.. Why it helps the audience is stated.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating neighbour on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with neighbour, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept original work about neighbour with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material. / Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for neighbour. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for neighbour. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Answers depend on the atlas (e.g","Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood","A claim that names no evidence from the lesson material","A method that skips the key step taught in this lesson"],"question":"Using an atlas, name three neighbouring countries or territories of Australia and the water body that separates Australia from one of them. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for neighbour; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Answers depend on the atlas (e.g","Careful use of Asia and explain why it matters with clear evidence","Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood","Australia’s neighbours in Asia and the Pacific include countries and island nations across water borders"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with neighbour?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named Asia and explain why it matters, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Apply neighbour to new material and name the Asia and explain why it matters used","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence","Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood","Name Asia and explain why it matters only, without linking it to neighbour"],"question":"Which response best applies neighbour with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The stronger choice uses sources, places or historical/geographic evidence appropriately for this lesson on neighbour. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Answers depend on the atlas (e.g","Make a bigger claim without naming any source or place detail","Copy a classmate’s sentence with no local detail","Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood"],"question":"Which response best uses sources, places or historical/geographic evidence for neighbour?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Strong answers name specific evidence and what it shows. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Copy a classmate’s sentence with no local detail","Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood","Name a specific source or place detail and say what it shows about neighbour","Make a bigger claim without naming any source or place detail"],"question":"Which evidence move best supports a claim about neighbour?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The stronger choice matches the taught idea (Australia’s neighbours in Asia and the Pacific include countries and) with concrete detail. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Make a bigger claim without naming any source or place detail","Copy a classmate’s sentence with no local detail","Example: using an atlas, students list nearby countries such as Indonesia, Papua New Guinea, New Zealand and Pacific","Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about neighbour?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Accuracy means checking evidence and honouring limits or protocols. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Invent missing details to make the answer sound complete","Ignore safety or cultural protocols to finish faster","Treat every claim as equally reliable without checking a source or cue","Check facts, acknowledge limits of the evidence, and avoid inventing details"],"question":"Which action keeps sources, places or historical/geographic evidence accurate for neighbour?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Independence requires a new example that still uses the taught skill. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Retype the worked example with no new example","Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood","Name Asia and explain why it matters only, with no linked example","Make a neighbours fact strip: five places from an atlas with direction from Australia and one shared link (trade"],"question":"Which independent response best applies neighbour to new material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about neighbour with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating neighbour on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using neighbour on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for neighbour. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea.","question":"Name one likely error with neighbour, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Sample error: Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood.. Correction: Answers depend on the atlas (e.g.. Why it helps the audience is stated.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent evidence and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-hsie-y4-w12-l1","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA HSIE alignment using catalogue outcome codes (HS2-*); content-point mapping and local First Nations protocols remain pending human review.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise neighbour.","Read the mission before you start mapping or using sources.","Keep the place, people or source you are studying in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your evidence with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the source or place detail that carries the idea.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore sources or respectful practice.","Prefer accurate evidence over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your evidence and reason are both present.","Proofread names, places, dates and sequence.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact source detail or place feature before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key evidence.","Say what each source or place detail shows about the idea.","A final label alone is weaker than recorded evidence."],"teach2":["Compare a weak claim with stronger evidence.","Change the claim or use of sources, not only how neat the poster looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh place, person or source that still uses the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original evidence and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new sources or places."]},"subject":"Geography","success_criteria":["I can use neighbour with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify Asia and explain why it matters.","I can practise Pacific independently on a new prompt.","I can notice region needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Australia’s neighbours in Asia and the Pacific include countries and island nations across water borders.","options":["A claim unrelated to the source or place","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no evidence","Australia’s neighbours in Asia and the Pacific include countries and island nations across water borders"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about neighbour with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: using an atlas, students list nearby countries such as Indonesia, Papua New Guinea, New Zealand and Pacific island nations (as shown on their map). They note ocean distances, not land borders, for many links.\n\nTRY FIRST\nUsing an atlas, name three neighbouring countries or territories of Australia and the water body that separates Australia from one of them.\n\nFEEDBACK\nAnswers depend on the atlas (e.g. Indonesia, PNG, New Zealand); water e.g. Timor Sea / Coral Sea / Tasman Sea as appropriate.","explain":"Australia’s neighbours in Asia and the Pacific include countries and island nations across water borders. Neighbours are identified with atlases; relationships include trade, travel and shared environments.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner base claims on sources, places and respectful community knowledge, rather than guessing from a single picture. Keep every claim linked to evidence.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a detail is uncertain, identify what source you would need next. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Calling every nearby place “Asia” without Pacific nations ignores the Pacific neighbourhood. Correct the claim or use of sources, not just the neatness of the poster.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Australia and neighbours.","caption":"Include Pacific nations.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Neighbours</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">Asia–Pacific</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Water links</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">not always land borders</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which source or place detail matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Example: using an atlas, students list nearby countries such as Indonesia, Papua New Guinea, New Zealand and Pacific isl Then write your own evidence.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which source or place detail matters most.\nJuno: Name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: Example: using an atlas, students list nearby countries such as Indonesia, Papua New Guinea, New Zealand and Pacific isl Then write your own evidence."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Make the HSIE idea visib